Z||000002||lawrence||08-27-2000||07:59 PM||||I made it.  It's the bottom of a front bumper, turned upside down.  This picture makes it obvious:<P> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe/98/4/ffront.gif" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe/98/4/ffront.gif</A> <P>I had been looking for an air dam plus a place to put driving lights.  While working under the car one day, the idea hit me.<P>There's a small write-up about it in one of the issues of my mag:<P> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe/99/1/tte.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe/99/1/tte.htm</A> <P>If you don't put the light buckets in, then it's almost a bolt-on.<P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe</A>  - WebElectric Magazine||||reg||1
